From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8650: add a PCIe suspend OPP

Give pcie0 a suspend-only OPP so pcie-qcom keeps a nonzero DDR/LLCC
sleep-set vote once the CPU subsystem collapses in s2idle. Without one,
pcie-qcom votes 0/0 on the PCIe memory path during suspend; SM8550 and
SM8750 reset instead of waking when nothing else votes DDR in the sleep
set. Give SM8650 the same floor.

Ported from Armada: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/410bcf26a67f3e5d38e487d0ec84c5632f2bc3f6/packages/kernel/patches/0527-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8650-add-a-pcie-suspend-opp.patch
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
@@ -3761,6 +3761,17 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 					opp-level = <3>;
 				};
+
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only: the synthetic opp-hz and missing opp-level
+				 * keep link-speed matching from selecting it.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcieport0: pcie@0 {
